%T A398822 232,248,250,264,270,280,296,297,312,320,328,343,344,351,375,376,378,
%U A398822 408,424,440,448,456,459,472,488,512,513,520,536,552,568,584,594,616,621,632
%N A398822 Numbers whose powerful part (A057521) is a cube that is larger than 1.
%C A398822 Nonsquarefree numbers such that every exponent in their prime factorization is either 1 or a multiple of 3.
%C A398822 Each term in this sequence has a unique representation as the product of two coprime numbers: a squarefree number and a cube that is larger than 1.
%C A398822 The asymptotic density of this sequence is zeta(3) * Product_{p prime} (1 - 1/p^2 - 1/p^4 + 1/p^5) - 1/zeta(2) = 0.0846412709905975115781... .
%H A398822 Amiram Eldar, <a href="/A398822/b398822.txt">Table of n, a(n) for n = 1..10000</a>
%H A398822 <a href="/index/Eu#epf">Index entries for sequences computed from exponents in factorization of n</a>.
%e A398822 24 = 2^3 * 3 is a term since its powerful part, 8 = 2^3, is a cube that is larger than 1.
%t A398822 q[k_] := Module[{e = FactorInteger[k][[;; , 2]]}, AnyTrue[e, # > 1 &] && AllTrue[e, # == 1 || Divisible[#, 3] &]]; Select[Range[650], q]
%o A398822 (PARI) isok(k) = if(k == 1, 0, my(e = factor(k)[, 2]); vecmax(e) > 1 && #select(x -> (x > 1 && x%3), e) == 0);
%Y A398822 Intersection of A013929 and A398818.
%Y A398822 A398818 is a disjoint union of A005117 and this sequence.
%Y A398822 Subsequences: A048109, A398823.
%Y A398822 Cf. A000578, A002117, A057521, A059956.
